>> title: Papadom
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: indian, lentils, fried, cracker, starter
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: papadum, poppadom, poppadum, pappadam, papad, appalam
>> pairs-with: mango-chutney, lime-pickle, mint-chutney, kachumber
>> servings: 8
>> time: 8 hr
>> slack: narrow — the fry is twenty seconds a side: it blisters and then it burns, with no in-between and nothing to do once it darkens

>> step: mix to a very stiff dough
Mix @urad dal flour{2%cup}(240 g), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @asafoetida{1/4%tsp}, @black peppercorns{2%tsp}(coarsely cracked), @baking soda{1/4%tsp} and @water{1/3%cup}(80 mL) in a #bowl{} to a dough far stiffer than you think can be right.

>> step: knead 10 min, until it goes glassy
Knead @&(~1)stiff dough{} with @neutral oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) ~knead{10%min}, on a board, leaning into it, until it turns from crumbs to something smooth and faintly glassy.

>> step: rest 30 min under a cloth
Rest @&(~1)dough{} under a damp cloth ~rest{30%min}.

>> step: roll paper-thin, dry 6 hr
Roll @&(~1)dough{} in walnut-sized balls out to 7-inch rounds you can read through, then ~dry{6%hr} on a rack in the sun or a fan, turning once, until they snap.

>> step: fry 20 sec a side, until it blisters and stops bubbling
Fry @&(~1)dried rounds{} one at a time in @neutral oil{4%cup}(950 mL) at 375°F (190°C) ~fry{20%sec}, holding them flat with tongs for the first three seconds so they do not curl into a taco.

They can go dry into a very hot pan or straight onto a gas flame for fifteen seconds a side.
